    "body": "Problem:\r\ngitsendemail sources only ftplugin/mail.vim, skipping Lua mail ftplugins in runtimepath.\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\nSource both mail.vim and mail.lua.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSince the mail.vim file is so small I opted to just edit it directly, but perhaps having the extra code in a gitsendemail.lua is preferred? I'm also not sure if I should change the file-top comments, like 'Last Change'?",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-12T14:02:35Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "These files are owned by vim/vim, so please don't edit them directly. \r\n\r\nAlso, this issue applies to a large number of ftplugins, so I don't think a single file solution is the way to go here.\r\n\r\nWould you mind opening an issue about this instead so we can discuss a more general solution?",
